{
  "rationale": "This is the final iteration, so the candidate should be the best-measured design rather than an untested change. Iteration 10 raced the Evaluator-approved configuration (entityR1: the iteration 8 geometry with base_speed 1.2) and scored 125.48, the best so far. Compared with iteration 8 (base_speed 1.4, score 123.04), the per-track results were mixed. Progress on the s-bend rose from 0.24 to 0.34, which is the gain the plan wanted. Oval progress fell from 0.57 to 0.51, which by the agreed rule would have sent speed back to 1.4. Slalom progress fell from 0.09 to 0.07 and its mean score dropped from 38.3 to 29.4. The aggregate still favoured 1.2, and the s-bend gain is the larger of the two per-track changes. Oval max_error stayed at 0.064, still just over the 0.06 limit, and steering_oscillation stayed high at about 0.27. Every trial on every track still went off track. Because the unseen final track has a different shape, I am not adding changes that the development tracks have not tested. Sensors stay at x = ±0.030 m with 16 mm footprints, kp 6.0, kd 0.6, ki 0.05, sensor weights (-1, -0.5, 0, 0.5, 1) and line_loss last_direction. Geometry and gains are unchanged from the best-supported configuration. The only controller difference from iteration 8 is base_speed 1.2, which the approved candidate proposed and which measured best overall. Expected result: a score close to the 125 measured in iteration 10, with s-bend progress staying above 0.3 and oval progress near 0.5. Hypotheses to check: (1) at 1.2, the s-bend line losses (1.7 in iteration 10 against 1.3 at 1.4) come from the slower base speed making bend entries less stable, not from sensing reach. (2) Oval max_error near 0.064 is still set by the first large offset at bend entries rather than by gain. Measurements requested: per-track progress, max_error, line_loss_events, steering_oscillation, rms_error and control_effort, so the next evidence shows whether the s-bend and oval results hold on a new layout.",
